{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122322-vitae-addiction","id":1122322,"title":"Vitae addiction","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-29T06:47:39-07:00","id":1122322,"title":"Vitae addiction","content":"The rule for getting vitae addiction is a bit meh. So the number of blood points is the penality for your resistance roll. My whole gripe with this, that\u00b4s not at all how addiction works. A greater dosis doesn\u00b4t make for a greater chance to get addicted, it is more the frequently use that makes you addicted. So I\u00b4m thinking:<br /> <br /> 1) Cap that penality to -2. It\u00b4s not really realistic, but it comes closer than vanilla rules.<br /> 2) Maybe a -1 penality for everytime you drink, with a reset after loosing one humanity point? Got my gripes with this, since it guarantees Vitae addiction when you drink s few times Kindred Vitae from a vampire and it\u00b4s additional bookkeeping.<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13653-narr666","name":"Narr666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T07:02:11-07:00","id":1122325,"title":"","content":"Vitae Addiction is something mystical and isn't supposed to work like regular addictions. But if you want to make it mundane I agree that the quantity penalty should have a low cap. Other than that you'd need to define a load of situational modifiers. Living a shitty life (low living standards, belonging to a marginalized group, suffering from mental illnesses, etc) is far more relevant for developing addictions than the addictive quality of a drug.<br /> <br /> Edit: Along with continued exposure, of course, like your second point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 07-29-2017, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T07:19:20-07:00","id":1122329,"title":"","content":"Hey Tessie,<br /> <br /> maybe I expressed it not the right way. I don\u00b4t seek for a real simulation on addiction (and I agree with you that addiction has more factors than the mere use). It just doesn\u00b4t feel right, that a Vampire is more likely to be addicted only if he has drank more Vitae in one go. That is also for gameplay reasons: Grabbing and drinking from a Vampire is in my opinion a valid tactic in combat, but 5 Vitae would almost guarantee an addiction. It really does not feel mystical if your Vitae addiction comes because you drank much of it in one go.<br /> Thanks for the feedback. I will likely take your advice and test the second option.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13653-narr666","name":"Narr666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T17:45:17-07:00","id":1123251,"title":"","content":"Instead of amount, you could cue the penalty to Blood Potency, making stronger / sweeter blood more addictive. I'd make the modifier the difference in blood potency between the two. Easier to shrug off addiction to Vampires with lower BP, tougher to shrug off drinking from someone higher than you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T05:26:43-07:00","id":1123414,"title":"","content":"Think of Vitae addiction like a snare or a trap, the more potent it is the more likely it would capture a prey. It doesn't work like your everyday heroin addiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T13:51:07-07:00","id":1123621,"title":"","content":"i like the idea of repeated exposure and higher blood potency (of vitae drunk) increasing the chance of vitae addiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T15:17:26-07:00","id":1126468,"title":"","content":"I like the idea with the Blood Potency. So what about giving an malus equal the difference of blood potency, making a victim with less potency giving a malus from zero. Than you can combine it by making repeated attempts more difficult?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13653-narr666","name":"Narr666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T11:38:10-07:00","id":1127220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Narr666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122322-vitae-addiction?p=1126468#post1126468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea with the Blood Potency. So what about giving an malus equal the difference of blood potency, making a victim with less potency giving a malus from zero. Than you can combine it by making repeated attempts more difficult?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Repeated attempts like the cumulative penalty for retrying a task? That sounds very reasonable. I would have the penalty count up after each attempt, possible with a cool-down time that causes it to decrease if I wanted to create an ebb and flow/cyclic mood in relation to Blood Addition or possibly just slowing increasing and never decreasing until they are &quot;cured&quot; by requiring vampire Vitae to subsist if I wanted emphasis an ever mounting pressure motif. I also like the difference between Blood Potency being a factor.<br /> <br /> Those two together look like this:<br /> <br /> +4 through -9 for Blood Potency Modifiers (only +4 because at BP 6 you gain immunity to Blood Addition)<br /> 0 through -5 for cumulative attempts to resist.<br /> <br /> that comes together to a range of +4 to -14 With a BP 5 feeding from from a BP 1 for the first time on one end and a BP 1 feeding from a BP 10 for the 6th or greater time at the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 08-10-2017, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T13:26:47-07:00","id":1127281,"title":"","content":"The cooldown or reset could be tied to loosing one humanity point. That could make the bookkeeping simpler","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13653-narr666","name":"Narr666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}